---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import ButtonRow from '../components/ButtonRow.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import type { Locale } from '../i18n/ui';

interface Props {
  locale: Locale;
}

const { locale } = Astro.props;
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Six years of backend work across the Israeli and Ukrainian markets — payments, order lifecycles, production workflows — and the tooling built to keep AI-assisted engineering honest."
  current="/about"
  locale={locale}
  ogCard="about"
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label">About</p>
      <h1>The person</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Six years of backend work, most of it on systems where a wrong answer costs somebody money.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Section
    label="Career"
    title="Where the work happened"
    lead="Employers are named. Clients are not — three of the four case studies sit under NDA, and none of them is tied to a period or a company here."
  >
    <ol class="timeline">
      {
        site.timeline.map((job) => (
          <li>
            <div class="when">
              <span class="num">{job.from}</span>
              <span class="num">{job.to}</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>{job.role}</h3>
              <p class="org">
                {job.org} — {job.note}
              </p>
              <ul>
                {job.highlights.map((h) => (
                  <li>{h}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </Section>

  <Section
    label="Markets"
    title="Israel and Ukraine"
    lead="Two markets with very different assumptions, which is most of why the work got interesting."
  >
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The Israeli work meant Hebrew and right-to-left products, Israeli fintech and accounting
        systems, and telephony that has to speak to people rather than at them. Right-to-left is
        where most implementations quietly break: text has to be passed in logical order, because
        reordering happens per display line <em>after</em> wrapping — a paragraph reversed in advance
        reads bottom-up the moment it wraps.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Ukrainian work was commerce and integration at volume: catalogue sync with an ERP, local
        payment and delivery providers, and platforms cloned per market without forking the
        codebase.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Languages" title="How I communicate">
    <dl class="langs">
      {
        site.languages.map((l) => (
          <div>
            <dt>{l.name}</dt>
            <dd>{l.level}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
    <p class="prose note">
      Working language on a team is English. Documentation, specs, commit messages and API contracts
      are written in English regardless of who is reading them, because the next person to open the
      repository may not share a first language with anyone currently on it.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section
    label="Leading"
    title="How I run a team"
    lead="Mostly by making the standard checkable, so it survives the week I am not looking."
  >
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I set the engineering standards and the Definition of Done, and then I put them in tooling
        rather than in a wiki page. Groundwork exists because a review checklist that lives in
        somebody’s head is a checklist that gets skipped under deadline — and because an AI agent
        will report success with exactly the same confidence whether or not it succeeded.
      </p>
      <p>
        The part that took longest to learn is that the process has to scale down. A typo and a
        change to how VAT is calculated do not deserve the same ceremony, and applying the heavy
        version to everything is how a process stops being used at all.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section
    label="Next"
    title="What I want next"
    lead="A Senior Backend or Tech Lead role on a product with real domain weight."
    last
  >
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Payments, order lifecycles, production workflows, applied AI that has to survive contact
        with production — those are the problems I am good at and the ones I want more of. Remote
        worldwide, or relocation. {site.availability.split('·').slice(-1)[0]?.trim()}.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ButtonRow>
      <Button
        href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent(site.contact.emailSubject)}`}
      >
        {site.contact.email}
      </Button>
      {/* The CV stays English in every locale — see the note in Header.astro. */}
      <Button href="/cv" variant="outline">Read the CV</Button>
    </ButtonRow>
  </Section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-head {
    padding: var(--space-10) 0 var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: var(--rule) solid var(--border);
  }

  .page-head h1 {
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 var(--space-5);
    font-size: var(--display-l);
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 34ch;
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
  }

  .timeline {
    padding: 0;
    border-top: var(--rule) solid var(--border);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .timeline > li {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    padding: var(--space-6) 0;
    border-bottom: var(--rule) solid var(--border);
  }

  @media (min-width: 52rem) {
    .timeline > li {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 10rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-8);
    }
  }

  .when {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  .timeline h3 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
  }

  .org {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--accent-text);
  }

  .timeline ul {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .timeline ul li {
    padding: var(--space-2) 0;
    border-bottom: var(--rule-thin) solid var(--border);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  .timeline ul li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .langs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(12rem, 1fr));
    border-top: var(--rule) solid var(--border);
    border-left: var(--rule) solid var(--border);
  }

  .langs > div {
    padding: var(--space-5);
    border-right: var(--rule) solid var(--border);
    border-bottom: var(--rule) solid var(--border);
  }

  .langs dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .langs dd {
    margin: var(--space-1) 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-2xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-text);
  }

  .note {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
</style>
